# 📚 Today's Topic

**Functions with Multiple Parameters**

### 🌟 Why are we learning this?

Many real programs need more than one value to complete a task.
Multiple parameters let a function receive different pieces of information at the same time.

---

# 📖 Learn Before You Code

## What is it?

A function can have two or more parameters.
Each parameter receives its own value when the function is called.
This makes one function useful in many situations.

## Why do programmers use it?

Think of filling out a school form. You enter your name, class, and roll number together. A function can also receive several values at once.

## Real-Life Example

A food delivery app needs your address, phone number, and order details before it can deliver your meal.

## Important Points

- A function can have many parameters.
- Parameters are separated by commas.
- Values are passed in the same order.
- Multiple parameters reduce repeated code.
- Functions stay organised and reusable.

> 💡 **Remember:** Pass values in the correct order unless you use keyword arguments later.

## Common Beginner Mistake

Passing fewer or more values than the function expects.

## Tiny Summary

Multiple parameters help one function work with several related values together.

